    'State the mistaken universalization or ratio replacement that leads to a=0 for every sequence, not only the zero-ratio first-term error.'],
  ['q712-nesting', 'C', 'CEILING-ZERO-BOUNDARY',
    'Upward rounding/ceiling of a fractional part yields 1 for a strictly positive fractional part, but yields 0 when the input is an integer and its fractional part is 0. C asserts value 1 for every real input. The authored procedure therefore fails exactly at the integer boundary needed to generate the universal false claim; rounding zero to the next integer would be a different procedure requiring explicit disclosure.',
